71 "Consider the matrices given below. Given that $A$ and $B$ are row equivalent matrices and $det(A)=6$, find $det(B).$\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -5 & 6 & 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -2 & -1 \\\\ -5 & 6 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186483371 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5c8f03a1-964a-5fd4-a60f-a2aa229186e2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186483371 #edb/ref 1074 "Notice that $B$ can be obtained from $A$ by swapping the $2$nd and the $3$rd rows. \n\nThis changes the sign of the determinant to the opposite one.\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =-det(A) \\\\  & =-(6) \\\\  & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497909 #edb/ref 1080 "-12" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497909 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497909 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "33b25027-8221-5098-9167-254d753c3213" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497989 #edb/ref 1080 "-18" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497989 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186497989 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4f11998a-ad24-5209-8a9f-c63c403858e6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498017 #edb/ref 1080 "-24" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498017 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498017 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5bda7aff-8f4a-54a5-aebf-3a9be4dd94f1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498148 #edb/ref 1080 "24" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498148 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498148 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "9a175c4f-3333-5a30-a0ee-942d881a95f5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498254 #edb/ref 1080 "18" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498254 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498254 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "cb8dc81a-a234-558b-87aa-921ac69d0c23" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498398 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186497909 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498398 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186497989 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498398 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186498017 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498398 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186498148 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498398 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186498254 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498398 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498398 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498398 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186498017 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498398 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "594aa2c5-6ab3-59e0-94ef-12b55bd75a5d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498488 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186498398 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498488 #edb/ref 1069 "q-130768" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498488 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498488 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix and $det(A)=6.$ The matrix $B$ is obtained from $A$ by applying the elementary row operations ${R}_{2}↔{R}_{3}$ and ${R}_{3}:=4{R}_{3}.$ What is the value of $det(B)?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498488 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "023c52b0-f119-5895-8d3f-31a9468a20b5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186498488 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's figure out what each operation does to the determinant.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{2}↔{R}_{3}$ involves swapping two rows, so it changes the sign of the determinant to the opposite one.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{3}:=4{R}_{3}$ involves multiplying a row by $4,$ so the determinant is multiplied by $4$ as well.\n\nTherefore, we have to change the sign of the determinant to the opposite one and multiply by $4$ as well. Consequently, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =4\\cdot (-det(A)) \\\\  & =-4det(A) \\\\  & =-4\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =-24.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
